\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Dataset-level effect of the deterministic deployment rule. Each row is one of the 12 evaluation datasets; the hollow marker is gating+fusion and the filled marker is DCD. The line length is the gain; positive values indicate DCD is better. Dice gains are in percentage points and HD95 gains in pixels. Unseen datasets are above the dashed line, Novel datasets below it. DCD improves Dice on 8/12 datasets and HD95 on 4/12; the large HD95 gain on TopoMortar contrasts with HD95 losses on several other datasets. Absolute values are reported in Table~5; all values are four-seed means.}}{8}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dcd_deployment}{{3}{8}{Dataset-level effect of the deterministic deployment rule. Each row is one of the 12 evaluation datasets; the hollow marker is gating+fusion and the filled marker is DCD. The line length is the gain; positive values indicate DCD is better. Dice gains are in percentage points and HD95 gains in pixels. Unseen datasets are above the dashed line, Novel datasets below it. DCD improves Dice on 8/12 datasets and HD95 on 4/12; the large HD95 gain on TopoMortar contrasts with HD95 losses on several other datasets. Absolute values are reported in Table~5; all values are four-seed means}{figure.caption.8}{}}
\newlabel{fig:dcd_deployment@cref}{{[figure][3][]3}{[1][5][]8}{}{}{}}
